OpenTS for RISC OS
==================

Preview release

Command & Conquer: Tiberian Sun (1999) and its Firestorm expansion, for
RISC OS. OpenTS is a community-led, open-source reconstruction of the
game's engine: a new program, not the original executable. It is based on
the source code Electronic Arts released under the GNU GPL for other
Command & Conquer games, and on reverse engineering of Tiberian Sun.

OpenTS:          https://github.com/OpenTS-Developers/OpenTS
OpenTS manual:   https://opents-developers.github.io/OpenTS/
RISC OS port:    https://github.com/davidpsharp/OpenTS (branch riscos)

This RISC OS version is a port of OpenTS, ported by David Sharp. It needs
RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi (it doesn't run on a Risc PC). It draws
everything in software, since RISC OS has no 3D drivers, and runs full
screen. Its source code, updates and bug reports for the port are at the
RISC OS port address above.

The main menu shows the version and the build it was made from.


Requirements
------------

  * A Raspberry Pi with RISC OS 5, tested on RISC OS 5.30. A Pi 4 is
    best; it also runs on a Pi 2 and a Pi 3, more slowly.
  * These modules, which come with RISC OS 5 or from PackMan, in !System:
      SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later
      ARMEABISupport 1.03 or later
      DigitalRenderer, for sound (without it the game is silent)
  * About 250 MB of disc space for the game data, plus about 1.4 GB if
    you want all the movies.


Installing the game data
------------------------

The game data isn't included. You need the freeware Tiberian Sun CD
images that Electronic Arts released in 2010. There are three discs, and
no CD key is needed:

  GDI disc        the game itself, the GDI campaign and its movies
  Nod disc        the Nod campaign and its movies
  Firestorm disc  the Firestorm expansion: its two campaigns, its movies
                  and its extra skirmish and multiplayer maps

The GDI disc is needed. Without the Nod disc the Nod campaign can't be
played (the GDI campaign, Firestorm, skirmish and multiplayer games can
all still be), and without the Firestorm disc only Tiberian Sun itself
can be played. All three are best.

As of October 2026 they can be downloaded from cnc-comm.com:

  GDI disc:        https://cnc-comm.com/tiberian-sun/downloads/the-game/gdi-disc
  Nod disc:        https://cnc-comm.com/tiberian-sun/downloads/the-game/nod-disc
  Firestorm disc:  https://cnc-comm.com/tiberian-sun/downloads/the-game/firestorm-disc

The downloads are zip files (TS_GDI.zip, TS_Nod.zip and TS_Firestorm.zip),
each holding one .iso file of about 700 MB. Unzip them first; that's
easiest on a modern computer, since a zip and its ISO together need about
1.3 GB. If you are short of space, install one disc at a time: unzip it,
run Prepare, then delete the ISO before the next.

The Prepare file that comes next to !OpenTS installs the data from the ISO
files:

  1. Put !OpenTS where you want to keep the game, and open the directory
     containing it, so the Filer has seen it.
  2. Copy Prepare into the directory holding the ISO files. They don't
     need to be on the same disc as !OpenTS.
  3. Double-click Prepare.

Prepare reads the ISO files directly (no CD drive or CDFS is needed),
copies the game files into !OpenTS and checks each one against the
freeware discs' checksums. It recognises the images by their contents,
so it doesn't matter if RISC OS has shortened their names. Files already
installed are skipped, so it's safe to run it again.

From the command line you can also name the images and give options:

  *Obey SDFS::RISCOSpi.$.ISOs.Prepare -nomovies
  *Obey SDFS::RISCOSpi.$.Prepare SDFS::RISCOSpi.$.Downloads.CD1_GDI/iso

  -nomovies  leaves out the movies (MOVIES01.MIX, MOVIES02.MIX and
             MOVIES03.MIX, about 1.4 GB together)
  -force     rewrites files that are already there

Without the movies the game skips them. If you added the GDI disc first
and the Nod disc later, just run Prepare again with the Nod image: the
files already installed are skipped.

If you have the game data already, from the CDs or an installed copy, you
can copy the files into !OpenTS yourself instead: TIBSUN.MIX, MAPS01.MIX,
SCORES.MIX and SIDECD01.MIX from the GDI disc, MAPS02.MIX and SIDECD02.MIX
from the Nod disc, and EXPAND01.MIX, MULTI.MIX, WDTVOX.MIX, E01SCD01.MIX,
E01SCD02.MIX, MAPS03.MIX, SCORES01.MIX, SIDECD02.MIX and WDT.MIX from the
Firestorm disc (several are in its INSTALL directory; its MULTI.MIX and
SIDECD02.MIX are newer than the other discs' copies). The movies are
MOVIES01.MIX, MOVIES02.MIX and MOVIES03.MIX, one on each disc.


Playing
-------

Double-click !OpenTS to put its icon on the icon bar, then click the icon
to start the game and choose Tiberian Sun or Firestorm. The controls are
the original game's. In a game, move the pointer to the edge of the
screen to scroll the map. The mouse wheel scrolls the build columns in the
sidebar: over one column it scrolls just that one, elsewhere both.

The desktop doesn't respond while the game is on the screen. Shift+F12,
or Desktop in the game's Options menu, goes back to it, with the game
paused where it was (sound too); click the icon again to carry on. In a
network game the game carries on for the other players meanwhile. The
icon's menu has Info and Quit. Insert saves a screenshot, as a PNG file in
!OpenTS.Screenshots.

The first time it runs, the game picks its screen size for you: the shape
of your screen, as large as this computer can draw smoothly (it takes about
a second to time it). The game is then scaled to fill the screen. Larger
sizes show more of the map. To change the size, use Options, then Display,
on the main menu; to change it during a game, save the game, change the size
on the main menu, then load the game. To have the game pick again, for
instance after moving it to a faster computer, set this before running it:

  *Set OpenTS$Retune 1

Saved games are in !OpenTS.Saved Games. They can be moved between RISC OS
and OpenTS on other computers.


Problems
--------

The game writes a log to the Debug directory in !OpenTS, and its messages
go to !OpenTS.stderr. If something goes wrong, please include the newest
log and stderr in a bug report. To also log frame rates, set this before
running the game:

  *Set OPENTS_FPS 1

Known issues in this preview:

  * The end credits' text isn't drawn.
  * Network play has only been tried between two Pis on a local network
    (LAN).
  * A network game against OpenTS on another kind of computer (the Mac
    build has been tried) goes out of sync after a while, so play RISC OS
    against RISC OS.
  * The World Domination Tour needs Westwood's old online service, which
    has closed, so it doesn't start.


